# Strategic Direction (May 2026)

**This rule is the single most important piece of context for the codebase right now.** A major architectural shift decided in May 2026 is well underway: **Phase 1 (Web2 cleanup) and Phase 2 (selective-disclosure attestations) have shipped.** Phase 3 — the Midnight ZK backbone — is now an **active, go-to-market-driven track** (see "Phase 3 is an active track" below). Match every code change to the phase the project is actually in.

Master reference: `docs/midnight/ARCHITECTURE.md`. When this rule is ambiguous, that doc wins.

---

## What Storm is becoming

A **portable, composable Driver Qualification (DQ) file platform** for trucking, where verified credential facts are eventually backed by **selective-disclosure cryptographic proofs**. The moat is *selective disclosure of verified facts* — competitors (Tenstreet, HireRight, DriverFacts) cannot retrofit it without rebuilding their CRA business model.

The chain is never the moat itself — the moat is *selective disclosure of verified facts*. But "the chain is invisible" applies to **interaction, not narrative**. Users never *interact with* the chain: no wallet, no seed phrase, no gas, no signing. They may absolutely *read about* it — Provven celebrates Midnight / zero-knowledge / selective disclosure as its public credibility story (domain: `provven.com`; prior domains `zknight.io` / `stormchain.ai`). The split is **narrative (encouraged) vs. interaction (gated) vs. per-fact claim (provenance-gated)**. See `DECISION_LOG.md` DEC-2026-05-016.

