## What changed

### Old paradigm (still in code, not yet removed)
- Alchemy Account Kit smart wallets for auth (`x-wallet-address` header pattern in API routes)
- USDC payments via Base Sepolia (`MvrPaymentButton`, `PspPaymentButton`)
- IPFS document storage via Pinata (`lib/ipfs.ts`)
- On-chain hash registries (`ResumeRegistry`, `ProductionDriverRegistry`) on Base Sepolia
- STORM ERC-20 token (deployed to Sepolia, never live)
- "Blockchain verified" UI badges

### New paradigm (Phase 1 + 2)
- Email / Google / magic-link auth via **Supabase Auth** (locked 2026-05-22; uses `@supabase/ssr` for cookie sessions; sign-in UI built with Storm's `@/components/ui` primitives)
- Stripe Checkout (one-time) + Subscriptions for MVR / PSP / employer plans (Pace billing deferred per DEC-2026-05-006)
- Supabase Storage for documents
- No on-chain registries; verifications via `attestationService` interface
- STORM ERC-20 dropped on Base; replaced with off-chain `users.storm_points` ledger; Midnight reissue (likely shielded) preserved as Phase 3 optionality
- "Verified by Storm" UI (Phase 2, live) → "Verified on Midnight" UI (Phase 3, in progress — flip a per-fact on-chain claim only when that proof actually runs; see the honesty guardrail above)

### Phase 3 — active track (Midnight ZK)
- Midnight as the ZK target chain
- Compact contracts for credential-disclosure circuits
- Server-side proof server (managed Docker on Cloud Run / Render / Fly)
- Server-managed Midnight wallet for proof submission

The proof backend swaps in behind the existing `attestationService` interface — carrier-facing UX does not change. See "Phase 3 is an active track" above for *why now* and the non-negotiable quality bar.

